WEBVTT

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:03.700
I'm recording one, too?

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:07.250
I'm Funada Yurika.

00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:10.980
When you were born,

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:16.170
I never imagined the world 
would turn out like this.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.810
I wonder what I should talk about.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:25.690
How about the happiest thing in your life?
 And the saddest thing?

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:29.690
The happiest thing?

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:32.890
Well, that's obvious.

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:35.700
Giving birth to you.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:40.740
The saddest thing in my life...

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:45.210
would have been the day 
your father died, I suppose.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:50.440
I don't want anyone else to die before me.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:54.770
If anyone must die, 
I'd rather go before you do.

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:57.820
Come on, Mom,

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:00.700
don't say things like that!

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.510
<b>"Letter of Farewell"</b>

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:14.890
Ka..th...leen.

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:17.920
Mother?

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:25.830
Mother!

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.320
Why, you...!

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:11.120
There were still more damn lizards left?!

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:16.480
No, we don't know for sure yet.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:24.490
There is the off chance that lizard 
stabbed someone else in the last 24 hours,

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:26.160
which means we'll just have to pray

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:29.910
that Yurika happened to get hit 
with an empty stinger.

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:35.330
If that's the case,
 she won't become a Gibia, right?

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:38.900
Damn it!

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:41.480
<i>If only I'd...!</i>

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:46.160
For now, we need to let 
Sensui-kun get some rest.

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:49.780
We'll have everyone rest up here for today.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:50.880
Yeah.

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:08.570
Mom?

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:13.640
What's the matter?

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:15.830
My mom's...

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:18.410
My mom's not here!

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:24.960
If only I had noticed!

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:34.580
Okay, Ayame and I will head 
to the nearby apothecary for supplies

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:38.360
while we search for your mother.

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:46.360
Leave Sensui and Kathleen to me.

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:50.400
Old man, you going to be okay?

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:57.800
Quit your fretting and go without worry.

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:00.540
Big man here, calling it fretting!

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:02.290
Later, then!

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:20.880
Sensui, you have a terrible fever.

00:07:42.970 --> 00:07:44.560
<i>Dear Kathleen...</i>

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:52.800
<i>I'm truly sorry I couldn't stay 
with you until the end of your journey.</i>

00:07:53.820 --> 00:08:00.800
<i>I suppose this means you've now lost 
both your father and your mother.</i>

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:04.630
<i>But never forget:</i>

00:08:05.270 --> 00:08:08.760
<i>you still have Sensui-kun, Kenroku-kun,</i>

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:12.200
<i>Yukinojyo-san, and Ayame-chan with you.</i>

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:17.280
<i>They'll be sure to protect you, as well.</i>

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:23.100
<i>I'm positive Yoshinaga-san 
will develop a vaccine, too.</i>

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:31.530
<i>Every night comes to an end.</i>

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:37.140
<i>Remember what your father always said,</i>

00:08:37.820 --> 00:08:40.520
<i>and have faith that dawn will come.</i>

00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:45.810
I'll be praying for your happiness.

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:51.470
<i>If I don't become a Gibia 
after some time has passed,</i>

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:54.860
<i>I promise I'll come back.</i>

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:02.860
Mo...

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:06.770
Mom...

00:09:24.650 --> 00:09:26.650
Kathleen...

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:34.350
Please cheer up.

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:37.580
I know that might be impossible,

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:40.930
but please try.

00:09:42.170 --> 00:09:47.540
Ever since I found myself in this 
land where I have no connections,

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:53.300
your smile has been my one saving grace.

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:57.470
I won't ask you to smile,

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:01.800
and I'll do everything I can 
to keep you from feeling lonely.

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:05.930
So, could you please stop crying?

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:11.960
Okay.

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:21.910
Well, you know what's something else?

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:27.170
There was something that surprised me 
the most in this new world.

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:29.610
What?

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:35.500
How delicious that food 
called c-c-curry was

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:40.740
when they made it 
in that d-d-department store.

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:43.200
I've never had anything that tasted so good!

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:44.260
<b>Vegetable and Chicken 
Tomato Curry</b>

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:47.490
If we were able to eat something like 
that every day without starving to death,

00:10:47.490 --> 00:10:52.720
maybe no one would have had to 
kill each other in my era.

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:55.480
<i>That's right.</i>

00:10:56.640 --> 00:11:00.790
<i>These people have come 
from a much crueler time.</i>

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:05.980
<i>In their time, a person's life 
was much more fleeting.</i>

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:09.880
<i>I can't just wallow in sadness by myself.</i>

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:12.560
I'm sorry.

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:15.300
I know!

00:11:16.490 --> 00:11:21.030
My mother gave me this charm 
during my entrance exams,

00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:31.030
but I'm giving it to you.

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:34.080
Are you sure?

00:11:34.710 --> 00:11:37.430
This is precious to you, isn't it?

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:39.860
Yeah.

00:11:40.750 --> 00:11:44.270
So, in return, make sure you don't die.

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:48.870
I'll sew it into your clothes 
so you won't lose it.

00:11:58.600 --> 00:11:59.680
There it is!

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:05.350
My mom's sewing kit.

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:30.620
That does it!

00:12:34.110 --> 00:12:37.440
I knew it would look good 
on your chest near your heart.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:39.290
Heart?

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:41.380
I'll leave it to you.

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:46.970
Now I have the strength of a hundred men.

00:12:57.340 --> 00:13:03.410
All because I didn't notice the lizards...

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:06.280
Yurika-san...

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:14.410
Well, don't say that.

00:13:15.250 --> 00:13:21.510
Even women and children have to be able 
to protect themselves on the battlefield.

00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:25.560
You shouldn't stress yourself 
that much over it.

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:29.930
I'm sure her mother would feel the same way.

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:40.340
That old man looked like he was 
pretty upset over it, too.

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:44.050
Let's find some supplies and get back quick.

00:13:46.530 --> 00:13:47.770
Right.

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:50.460
We should head back soon.

00:14:26.490 --> 00:14:27.660
We're here.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:32.580
All right.

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:36.630
Let's hurry up and grab what 
we can, then head back.

00:14:37.110 --> 00:14:39.780
We didn't see Yukari-san, though.

00:14:43.970 --> 00:14:46.850
There are damned Gibia inside.

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:54.710
Looks like we'll have to fight.

00:14:56.940 --> 00:14:59.600
It's our first time 
fighting together, isn't it?

00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:01.090
Yeah.

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:02.640
You did great.

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:04.250
Yeah.

00:16:05.880 --> 00:16:06.680
Yeah.

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:33.190
Looks like there aren't any left.

00:16:42.190 --> 00:16:45.230
Here, some bandages and medical tape.

00:16:45.660 --> 00:16:46.700
Okay.

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:49.930
Some gauze, some antibacterial...

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:55.100
I don't understand this stuff.

00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:56.260
Oh!

00:16:56.810 --> 00:16:58.990
This is an antidote, right?

00:16:59.800 --> 00:17:01.950
That just leaves food.

00:17:02.460 --> 00:17:04.240
Let's split up and gather some.

00:17:04.240 --> 00:17:05.350
Got it.

00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:21.810
<i>Yurika-san.</i>

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:46.100
Hey, get it together!

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:50.010
We have to go look for the 
mother after we're done here.

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:56.240
With Sensui the way he is now, 
we have to stay on top of things.

00:17:58.620 --> 00:17:59.970
Right.

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:05.070
Okay, let's take the loot 
back to the old man.

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:09.310
Maybe the mother will already 
be back when we return.

00:18:09.790 --> 00:18:10.720
Yeah.

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:19.060
Big haul, big haul!

00:18:20.610 --> 00:18:22.850
We should be all right for a while with this.

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:24.210
Yeah.

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:39.800
This is...!

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:42.370
Sensui!

00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:13.400
<i>At a time like this?!</i>

00:19:25.420 --> 00:19:27.300
Yukinojyo-san, look.

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:30.830
There are so many.

00:19:35.420 --> 00:19:38.760
They're all returning to their nest 
before the sun comes up!

00:19:46.300 --> 00:19:49.280
<i>Sensui, I'll protect you!</i>

00:20:03.560 --> 00:20:05.110
Yukinojyo-san?!

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:14.310
Yukinojyo-san?

00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:24.000
Yukinojyo-san!

00:20:26.940 --> 00:20:28.930
Yukinojyo-san!

00:20:28.930 --> 00:20:30.430
Yukinojyo-san!

00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:32.960
Yukinojyo-san!

00:20:33.640 --> 00:20:35.390
Yukinojyo-san!

00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:37.830
Why?!

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:40.230
I'm going to fight, too, so open up!

00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:42.640
Yukinojyo-san!

00:20:49.490 --> 00:20:54.690
I'm sure this charm of yours 
will protect me, so I'll be fine!

00:20:55.420 --> 00:20:59.570
My time with you was enjoyable!

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:07.740
If I manage to return alive, 
could you make some c-c-curry for me again?

00:21:10.060 --> 00:21:12.300
The moon tonight

00:21:14.180 --> 00:21:18.020
is awfully red.

00:21:21.020 --> 00:21:23.230
You said you wouldn't...

00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:27.060
You said you wouldn't let me feel lonely!

00:21:32.740 --> 00:21:36.520
What's important is protecting your smile!

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:39.680
When there's someone I love,

00:21:40.460 --> 00:21:42.050
I can die for them!

00:21:49.960 --> 00:21:52.520
Come on, you Gibia!

00:21:52.520 --> 00:21:56.400
My name is Onikura Yukinojyo!

00:21:57.250 --> 00:22:03.270
A rakshasa even demons flee from!

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:09.720
<b>"Until It All Burns Away"</b>
